    read: "Hawkish hold, one dissenter more hawkish than June. The MPC held at 3.75% on 30 July by a 6–3 vote — Greene, Mann and Pill all dissenting for an immediate 25bp hike — a narrower margin than the 7–2 hold most economists expected, continuing the trend from a dovish cut-minority early in 2026 to this now three-strong hawkish bloc. The Bank's own Monetary Policy Report projects CPI peaking near 3.2% in Q4 2026, and the OIS/SONIA curve keeps pricing net tightening (~4.20% by end-2026, a ~4.2% peak by early 2027), with the November meeting seen as the more likely venue for a first hike than September. Berenberg and Oxford Economics both argue markets are overpricing the tightening and expect a hold well into 2027.",
